Fixed GRUB's `clinux`/`cinitrd` helper functions in the shipped `grub.cfg`, which checked the CPU architecture (`$grub_cpu`, always `x86_64`) instead of the firmware type (`$grub_platform`, `efi` vs `pc`) to decide between `linux`/`initrd` and `linuxefi`/`initrdefi`. This broke PXE boot for every legacy-BIOS GRUB client. Additionally, `linuxefi`/`initrdefi` are now only used when the `linuxefi` module is actually present, since some GRUB builds (e.g. recent `grub-efi-amd64-bin` on Ubuntu) no longer ship it at all and expect `linux`/`initrd` to be used directly even under EFI.
